From: zolotvok <zolotvok@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Don't fault when an async completion writes a freed IO_STATUS_BLOCK.

When a thread terminates with async I/O still pending, wineserver cancels
it (cancel_terminating_thread_asyncs) and queue_apc() redirects the
resulting APC_ASYNC_IO to another thread of the process, because the
issuing thread is TERMINATED. invoke_system_apc() on that other thread
then stores STATUS_CANCELLED into the IO_STATUS_BLOCK (usually the
caller's OVERLAPPED), whose memory may already be gone. If the APC was
delivered by SIGUSR1 into a wait, the store faults on the signal stack,
virtual_setup_exception() reports "nested exception on signal stack"
and abort_thread() kills the thread; for the main thread that ends the
process.

The NT kernel writes the user I/O status block under an exception
handler and silently ignores a fault there. Do the equivalent: before
storing the result of a deferred async completion, check that the
status block is still writable memory and drop the store otherwise.
Memory that Wine does not manage (no view) is only refused when it is
not mapped at all, so every case that did not crash before behaves as
before.

Seen with Watch Dogs 2 (Proton experimental-11.0 arm64, ARM64EC + FEX):
an IOCTL_NSIPROXY_WINE_CHANGE_NOTIFICATION (IPv4 unicast table, i.e.
NotifyAddrChange) issued with an OVERLAPPED at a high address; the
issuing thread exits, the cancel is delivered to the main thread, the
store hits an unmapped page, the game dies.

NOTE (Droid-Deck_Mali_Support): written without the Wine source tree at
hand (none is local); hunk context follows upstream Wine 10/11 and the
symbols present in the dist's ntdll.so (invoke_system_apc,
check_write_access, virtual_uninterrupted_write_memory). If a hunk does
not apply, apply it by hand: the change is one call in server.c, one
prototype, one function in virtual.c next to
virtual_uninterrupted_write_memory(). Use host_page_mask/page_mask,
whichever the tree has.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (keeper agent)
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c       |  2 +-
 dlls/ntdll/unix/unix_private.h |  1 +
 dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c      | 41 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 43 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
@@ -380,8 +380,8 @@ static void invoke_system_apc( const union apc_call *call, union apc_result *result, BOOL self )
         {
             result->async_io.status = status;
             result->async_io.total = info;
             /* the server will pass us NULL if a call failed synchronously */
-            set_async_iosb( call->async_io.sb, result->async_io.status, info );
+            virtual_set_async_iosb( call->async_io.sb, result->async_io.status, info );
         }
         else result->async_io.status = STATUS_PENDING; /* restart it */
         break;
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/unix_private.h
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/unix_private.h
@@ -290,5 +290,6 @@ extern BOOL virtual_check_buffer_for_write( void *ptr, SIZE_T size );
 extern SIZE_T virtual_uninterrupted_read_memory( const void *addr, void *buffer, SIZE_T size );
 extern NTSTATUS virtual_uninterrupted_write_memory( void *addr, const void *buffer, SIZE_T size );
+extern void virtual_set_async_iosb( client_ptr_t iosb, NTSTATUS status, ULONG_PTR info );
 extern void virtual_set_force_exec( BOOL enable );
 extern void virtual_set_large_address_space(void);
 extern void virtual_fill_image_information( const struct pe_image_info *pe_info,
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -4210,8 +4210,49 @@ NTSTATUS virtual_uninterrupted_write_memory( void *addr, const void *buffer, SIZE_T size )
     server_leave_uninterrupted_section( &virtual_mutex, &sigset );
     return ret;
 }
 
 
+/***********************************************************************
+ *           virtual_set_async_iosb
+ *
+ * Store the final status of a deferred async I/O completion (APC_ASYNC_IO).
+ *
+ * The completion may run long after the request was issued and on another
+ * thread: when the issuing thread terminates, the server cancels its asyncs
+ * and redirects the APC to any other thread of the process. The status block
+ * may be freed by then. Windows writes it under an exception handler and
+ * ignores a fault; skip the store instead of faulting (a fault here is often
+ * on the signal stack and kills the thread).
+ */
+void virtual_set_async_iosb( client_ptr_t iosb, NTSTATUS status, ULONG_PTR info )
+{
+    char *addr = wine_server_get_ptr( iosb );
+    size_t size = in_wow64_call() ? sizeof(IO_STATUS_BLOCK32) : sizeof(IO_STATUS_BLOCK);
+    char *start = ROUND_ADDR( addr, host_page_mask );
+    unsigned char vec[2];
+    BOOL has_write_watch = FALSE, writable;
+    sigset_t sigset;
+
+    if (!iosb) return;
+
+    server_enter_uninterrupted_section( &virtual_mutex, &sigset );
+    if (find_view( addr, size ))
+        writable = !check_write_access( addr, size, &has_write_watch );
+    else  /* not Wine-managed memory: refuse only if nothing is mapped there */
+        writable = !mincore( start, addr + size - start, vec );
+    if (writable)
+    {
+        set_async_iosb( iosb, status, info );
+        if (has_write_watch) update_write_watches( addr, size, size );
+    }
+    server_leave_uninterrupted_section( &virtual_mutex, &sigset );
+
+    if (!writable)
+        WARN( "status block %p is no longer writable, dropping status %#x info %#lx\n",
+              addr, (int)status, (long)info );
+}
+
+
 /***********************************************************************
  *           virtual_set_force_exec
  *
-- 
